{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540705-bene-ashmedai-2e","id":1540705,"title":"Bene Ashmedai 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-19T08:16:24-07:00","id":1540705,"title":"Bene Ashmedai 2e?","content":"I've been scouring the internet for 2nd Edition rules for the Bene Ashmedai in 2nd edition, and the best I could find was the Legacies - Rehashed homebrew document, which helped a lot, but I'm wondering if anyone has run this legacy in a game and what they decided the attainments should be.<br /> <br /> Also, the description of how 2nd Edition attainments work was....Really confusing. If someone has a &quot;explanation for dummies&quot; version of determining attainment dice/factors, I would really appreciate it. I recently joined a Mage game after having not played the game since first edition, and a lot of the changes have been difficult to follow. In addition, if there are some house rules that are recommended for running legacies/attainments, please let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2075,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","user":"Cardran","date":". 08-19-2024, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2075-cardran","name":"Cardran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T09:46:51-07:00","id":1540708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540705-bene-ashmedai-2e#post1540705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the description of how 2nd Edition attainments work was....Really confusing. If someone has a &quot;explanation for dummies&quot; version of determining attainment dice/factors, I would really appreciate it. I recently joined a Mage game after having not played the game since first edition, and a lot of the changes have been difficult to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attainments are constructed as spells with predefined Reach effects from a budget of the Attainment's rank plus one (as though the rank of the Attainment were the Arcanum rating of the spell being replicated), a bonus to the primary factor as normal, and the ability to assign additional spell factors (contextually not more of the primary factor, judging from the example) that would apply a penalty equal to the rating of the lowest Arcanum the Attainment uses (so multi-Arcanum Attainments are disincentivized).<br /> <br /> If an Attainment's Reach budget doesn't have anything allocated toward Casting Time, it takes a scene to cast; it doesn't require a roll to use and counts as having rolled successes equal to the mage's Arcanum rating for the purposes of effects that measure how many successes were rolled (this doesn't change the way spells that are Withstood work; those still compare Potency to Withstand as normal).<br /> <br /> Basically, Legacy Attainments are inflexible but reliable compared to spells, such that it's built as a spell when you get the Attainment and has its stats updated as your Arcanum ratings go up, you use it by declaring that you're using it, and if it's an effect that's Withstood you reduce its Potency by the target's Withstand rating; being free (or nearly so, in the case of Mana costs) of most of the drawbacks of a comparable spell is the price for this reliability, with greater power or variant utilization requiring the use of the spellcasting system to pump the spell factors or assign different Reach effects. If you understand how spell factors work, the above caveats just plug into that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T12:53:16-07:00","id":1540722,"title":"","content":"Sure thing, so the key details to keep in mind:<br /> <br /> 1) An Attainment has Reach available as if you were casting a spell with the equivalent Arcanum dots. So if your Time 1 Attainment is <i>Postcognition</i>, you have one Reach, since its the equivalent of casting it with Time 1. If its the third Attainment, Postcognition gets 3 Reach and 5 Reach if its the fifth Attainment. Meanwhile, <i>Temporal Stutter</i> could only be in the fourth or fifth Attainments, since it requires Time 4, having one Reach available if its in the fourth slot or two if its in the fifth. How the Reach is used is fixed when the Attainment is designed, so if you decided the <i>Postcognition </i>in the second Attainment slot would use instant use and advanced duration, it will always be so. Attainments cannot over Reach either, the inflexible Reach is the tradeoff for their reliability.<br /> <br /> 2) If an Attainment costs any amount of mana to cast, the total cost is truncated to one mana. So lets say you have Acceleration as your Time 4 Attainment. So you activate <i>Time in a Bottle</i>, then apply your Reach for advanced duration and rote property dodge. Normally you would pay two mana total (<i>Time in a Bottle</i> plus rote dodge), but since its an Attainment, you only pay one point of mana.<br /> <br /> 3) Any Attainments cast in ritual time always takes a scene to be used.<br /> <br /> 4) Attainments require no roll to use, you just declare you are using them, which means they are one of the most reliable options in your toolkit.<br /> <br /> 5) Attainments never provoke Quiescence or Breaking Points, so if you use a <i>Teleport</i> Attainment in front of a Sleeper, they will remember.<br /> <br /> 6) Attainments cost no spell slots and you always retain spell control. So if one Attainment makes zombies, for example, you can have as many zombies as you can make.<br /> <br /> 7) Attainment spell factors can be adjusted at casting time by using a number of pseudo-dice equivalent to the Arcanum's rating. So if you have Time 2, you can increase spell factors as if you had two dice to spend. With Time 4, you would have 4 pseudo-dice available and so on.<br /> <br /> Hope that proves helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-19T18:17:21-07:00","id":1540737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490341-diabolists-bene-ashmedai-2e-conversion\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490341-diabolists-bene-ashmedai-2e-conversion\"> Diabolists (Bene Ashmedai 2e Conversion) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490341-diabolists-bene-ashmedai-2e-conversion\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490341-diabolists-bene-ashmedai-2e-conversion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Bene Ashmedai Diabolists Pages 156-159 of The Silver Ladder for lore Doctrine and Magic Parent Path:Mastigos Parent Order: Silver Ladder Prerequisites: Spirit 2, Mind 1, Language (Hebrew), Meditative Mind Merit 1, Persuasion 2 and one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Empathy, Expression, Intimidation, </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Made this a while ago because I was gonna play one but that game fell through","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 08-19-2024, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-30T19:14:04-07:00","id":1541254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cardran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540705-bene-ashmedai-2e#post1540705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been scouring the internet for 2nd Edition rules for the Bene Ashmedai in 2nd edition, and the best I could find was the Legacies - Rehashed homebrew document, which helped a lot, but I'm wondering if anyone has run this legacy in a game and what they decided the attainments should be.<br /> <br /> Also, the description of how 2nd Edition attainments work was....Really confusing. If someone has a &quot;explanation for dummies&quot; version of determining attainment dice/factors, I would really appreciate it. I recently joined a Mage game after having not played the game since first edition, and a lot of the changes have been difficult to follow. In addition, if there are some house rules that are recommended for running legacies/attainments, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am using this setup, it is not the best possible combination (specially the adept level attainments) but I am working on improvements, and since this is a sister legacy of the Clavicularius, some of the attainments have the same name.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u><b>Bene Ashmedai</b></u></i><br /> <b>Parentage:</b> Mastigos or Silver Ladder<br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Spirit<br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Summoning circles (+1, +2 if made of exotic or expensive components); target is indulging a Vice (+1, +2 if it\u2019s the mage\u2019s Vice); the spell is cast in the service of others (+1); the spell is in keeping with your Vice (+1).<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Acting as a guru or other spiritual authority; conversing with goetic demons or other goeticists; demonological research; engaging in a seduction (either as the initiator or as the pursued); giving in to Vice without concern for the consequences (or inspiring another to do so); indulging in the fear and/or adulation of others; meditation on past moments of weakness; psychoanalyzing oneself or others.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiate </b>(<i>Diabolist\u2019s Circlet</i>)<br /> <u>Exorcist\u2019s Eye</u> - Instant Casting<br /> <u>Perfect Recall</u> - Instant Casting<br /> <br /> <b>Apprentice </b>(<i>Goetic Bulwark</i>)<br /> <u>Shadow Walk</u> - Advanced Duration<br /> <u>Alter Mental Pattern</u> - Advanced Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Disciple</b> (<i>Daimon\u2019s Measure</i>)<br /> <u>Ephemeral Shield</u> - Advanced Duration, &quot;Spirit\u2019s physical attacks&quot;<br /> <u>Mental Shield</u> - Advanced Duration, &quot;Goetia\u2019s physical attacks&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Adept </b>(<i>Goetic Struggle</i>)<br /> <u>Gossamer Touch</u> - Advanced Duration, &quot;Carried objects&quot;, &quot;Unarmed attacks&quot;<br /> <u>One Mind, Two Thoughts</u> - Advanced Duration, &quot;Instant Tasks&quot;, &quot;Physical Tasks in the Astral&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Master </b>(<i>Pandemonium\u2019s Mirror</i>)<br /> <u>Birth Spirit</u> - Advanced Duration<br /> <u>Psychic Genesis</u> - Advanced Duration\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> It is mainly focused on the defensive side, as befitting to those that usually indulge in Vice, they need to be protected from it. I also tried to get close to the original attainments described in 1ed, with a side of knowing other people weaknesses and Astral improvements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-19-2024, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-31T21:25:44-07:00","id":1541322,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\">I would like to propose an unorthodox approach to their Attainments.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Because they are more focused on understanding their vices and indulging them in a controlled manner, I thought they resonated more with the Thyrsus, so I inverted the Arcana.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Since they have a demonic influence in their origin, I also aimed to make their toolkit feel more unnerving, from their talent for quickly reading a situation, to their ability to influence the world around them without moving a muscle.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Lastly, I also tried to reinforce the design phrase from the original writeup: &quot;I am a prince amongst demons and a servant to men&quot;. This is what I have so far, please let me know what you think:</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Mind 1</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Passions drive everything, by opening their senses to the psychic imprints around them, the diabolist can read the emotional resonance around an object or perceive important events tied to a location. They are able to ask [Mind] yes or no questions about them to the Storyteller, or any of the following questions:</span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#333333\">What\u2019s the strongest emotion here?</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\">Who remembers this moment the most?</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\">Am I missing something in this scene?</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\">Where was this object during the event?</span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#333333\">What breaking point caused the event?</span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">This is a custom, Potency primary, Unveiling of Mind based on the </span><i><span style=\"color:#333333\">Psychometry </span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\">merit (</span><i><span style=\"color:#333333\">CofD</span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> page 58), with Reach assigned to instant use. Since it's an Unveiling, using sensory range is unneeded.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Spirit 1</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i>Exorcist's Eye</i></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"> with Reach assigned to advanced duration and conjunctional Mind allowing them to extend the benefits to goetia as well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The diabolist is keenly aware of the actions of those who would manipulate the emotional energy around them.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Mind 2</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i>Mental Scan</i></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"> with Reach assigned to instant use and reading surface thoughts. Since it's an Unveiling, using sensory range is unneeded.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The diabolist always sees through the facades people put up, peering into the true motivation behind their actions.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Spirit 2</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i>Coaxing the Spirits</i></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"> with Reach assigned to instant use and sensory range.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The diabolist needs only a thought to motivate the motes surrounding them into action.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Mind 3</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i>Know Nature</i></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"> with Reach assigned to instant use, sensory range and determining Aspirations and Obsessions.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">To one who delves deeply into understanding their own vices, reading those of others can be done at a glance.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Spirit 3</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">A combined spell of </span><i><span style=\"color:#333333\">Mental Shield</span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> and </span><i><span style=\"color:#333333\">Ephemeral Shield</span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\">, with Reach assigned to advanced duration and protecting from physical attacks. Two pseudo dice are used for the combined spell.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Mastering oneself requires the clarity to indulge one's vices free of outside influences.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><b>Mind 4</b></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#333333\">Emotional Urging</span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> with Reach assigned to instant use, sensory range and advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">Through their controlled self indulgence, the diabolist can fan or quell the flames of emotions in others.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><b>Spirit 4</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">A Potency primary Patterning of Mind and Spirit that creates a [lowest of Mind and Spirit] Retainer in Spirit Twilight by transforming some motes into a mind and using it to animate other ones, with its field being of the diabolist's choosing. Reach is assigned to advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">This is a Mind and Spirit variation of the </span><i><span style=\"color:#333333\">Golem </span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\">spell, used to create a better version of </span><i><span style=\"color:#333333\">Unseen Servant</span></i><span style=\"color:#333333\"> from D&amp;D. Similar to their own Vices, the diabolists shape the emotional energy around them into a powerful ally.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Mind 5</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i>Psychic Reprogramming</i></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"> with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">The greatest sign of mastery over oneself is to be able to define one's passions.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#333333\">Spirit 5</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><i>Familiar </i></span><span style=\"color:#333333\">with Reach assigned to indefinite duration, with a point of mana paying for indefinite duration and conjunctional Mind 4 allowing goetia to be bound as well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\">A prince of demons requires a court.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-01-2024, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}